  "details": "Come on, what the hell is going on with the design team? Why do I need an ESC Icon in the screen, or a clickable Mic Icon, if I have to press a key (ALT) to access it, WHEN pressing ESC already leads me to the Menu where the mic button actually is?\n\nThey're both ONE keypress of distance.\n\nIs VRChat targetting toddlers/elders gamers now? Because that's the only public I can imagine which wouldn't be able to know how to press ESC or how to mute/unmute themselves.\n\nIt really does not make sense in any practical way.\n\nSo, if I want to hide these useless things from my interface, I need to set the HUD opacity to 0, but... THAT ALSO HIDES THE NOTIFICATIONS! Seriously, what the hell is going on? I need to lose access to actual real-time useful informations in order to make my UI clean again?\n\nSo, if VRChat is choosing to keep that design, can we at least get the notifications settings separated from these? (like invites/join/groups announcements/etc)",
